# Allow-list of everything vendored into this repo from the working tree.
#
# Format:  <dest path in this repo>   <ROOT>:<source path under that root>   [edited:<reason>]
#          A trailing slash on BOTH sides means "this directory, recursively".
#          A line with no source is a file this repo OWNS; it is never synced.
# Roots:   TREE = $TOFU_TREE  (default /home/jack/tofu-unlearning)
#          HOME = $TOFU_HOME  (default /home/jack)
#          APA  = $APA_TREE   (default /home/jack/apa-uniform-sum)
#          MT7B = $MT7B_TREE  (default /home/jack/merge-tables-7b)
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
#
# WHY AN ALLOW-LIST AND NOT `rsync -a`:
# merge-tables-7b vendored the same tree with a blanket copy. Its own reproduce/VENDOR_DRIFT.md
# now records "52 files differ, 16 only in the repo, 220 only in home ... the repo copy is not a
# stale snapshot, it is a fork". A blind sync in either direction destroys real work. Only the
# paths below are ever copied, only ever tree -> repo, and `sync_from_tree.sh --check` reports
# drift without writing anything.
#
# EVERY vendored .py/.sh here carries `edited:deabsolutized` because the export rewrote each
# hard-coded /home/jack path into a repo-relative sibling lookup plus an env override (see
# PORTING.md). That is a permanent, intentional divergence: `--check` reports it as EDITED, not
# DRIFT, so a future sync is a deliberate merge rather than a silent overwrite of the port.

# ── the core tree ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tofu_sisa_lora/                 TREE:tofu_sisa_lora/                 edited:deabsolutized
log/                            TREE:log/

# ── routing projects ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ramole/                         HOME:ramole/                         edited:deabsolutized
legonet_lora/                   HOME:legonet_lora/                   edited:deabsolutized
sea/                            HOME:sea/                            edited:deabsolutized
sea_tofu/                       HOME:sea_tofu/                       edited:deabsolutized

# ── routerless selection (the paper's MUSR line and its neighbours) ──────────────────────────
sepmlp_tofu/                    HOME:sepmlp_tofu/                    edited:deabsolutized
blocktc_tofu/                   HOME:blocktc_tofu/                   edited:deabsolutized
memsinks_tofu/                  HOME:memsinks_tofu/                  edited:deabsolutized
memadapt_tofu/                  HOME:memadapt_tofu/                  edited:deabsolutized

# ── the APA / MUSR uniform-sum repo, whole ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
apa_uniform_sum/                APA:                                 edited:deabsolutized

# ── merge-tables-7b: ONLY the parts it owns. Its tofu_sisa_lora/, ramole/, legonet_lora/ and
#    external/ are a vendored duplicate of what this repo already carries first-hand.
merge_tables_7b/reproduce/      MT7B:reproduce/
merge_tables_7b/PLAN.md         MT7B:PLAN.md
merge_tables_7b/README.md       MT7B:README.md
merge_tables_7b/RESULTS_7B_K200.md   MT7B:RESULTS_7B_K200.md
merge_tables_7b/RESULTS_TABLES.md    MT7B:RESULTS_TABLES.md
merge_tables_7b/SETUP.md        MT7B:SETUP.md
merge_tables_7b/STATUS.md       MT7B:STATUS.md

# ── literature ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
papers/                         HOME:papers/

# ── the manuscript is DELIBERATELY ABSENT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# tofu_sisa_lora/paper/*.tex and the two AAAI PDFs were vendored, then removed when the GitHub
# repo turned out to be public: the submission is anonymized and under review, and its own notice
# forbids distribution. .gitignore keeps paper/pdf/ and paper/tex/ out. Originals stay in the
# working tree. paper/README.md (owned by this repo) carries the claim -> code map instead.

# ── the open-unlearning fork's UNCOMMITTED state. Not reachable from any git remote: it existed
#    only as a dirty working tree. Captured here or lost.
ou_integration/patches/sepmlp_registry.py        HOME:open-unlearning/src/model/sepmlp_registry.py   edited:deabsolutized
ou_integration/patches/SepMlp-Llama-3.2-1B.yaml  HOME:open-unlearning/configs/model/SepMlp-Llama-3.2-1B.yaml

# ── the site layer, taken from apa-uniform-sum (the most-ported copy) ────────────────────────
cluster_env.sh                  APA:cluster_env.sh                   edited:gpu-cap-clamp+ou-python
cluster_env.local.sh            APA:cluster_env.local.sh
cluster_env.sprint.sh           APA:cluster_env.sprint.sh
cluster_env.cispa.sh            APA:cluster_env.cispa.sh
slurm_nodes.sh                  APA:slurm_nodes.sh
stage_hf_cache.sh               APA:stage_hf_cache.sh

# ── files this repo OWNS (no source line — never synced, never overwritten) ──────────────────
# README.md
# SETUP.md
# PORTING.md
# STATUS.md
# PROVENANCE.md
# MANIFEST.files
# sync_from_tree.sh
# fetch_upstream.sh
# snapshot_results.py
# requirements-ou.txt
# test_repo_selfcontained.py
# paper/README.md
# ou_integration/patches/model__init__.diff   (generated by `git diff` against the fork)
# ou_integration/README.md
# results_snapshot/                            (generated by snapshot_results.py)
# .gitignore
